/**
 * @page termtests Terminal emulation tests
 *
 * @brief Screen-level regression tests that drive the real `botanik_sim` over a
 *        PTY and assert its reconstructed terminal against golden fixtures.
 *
 * The unit suite (@ref cpptests) checks logic in isolation; this suite checks what
 * the operator actually sees. It runs the real `botanik_sim` firmware over a
 * **PTY**, replays its ANSI output through [pyte](https://github.com/selectel/pyte)
 * to reconstruct the 80x24 screen, and asserts that screen against committed golden
 * fixtures. It catches terminal-rendering regressions - cursor moves, insert/delete,
 * IL/DL, the line editor's reconciliation - that a source diff cannot.
 *
 * Two design choices make it deterministic: a PTY (not a pipe) so the baud throttle
 * and TX back-pressure path are real, and time dilation via `BOTANIK_TIME_SCALE` so
 * a run is fast while every byte/event ratio matches a real 4800-baud session. The
 * suite is opt-in: CMake skips it unless pyte/pytest are importable.
 *
 * - @subpage md_tests_2pyte_2README - the full how-and-why: dependencies, the PTY
 *   and time-dilation rationale, the golden-fixture workflow, and how screens are
 *   normalised before comparison.
 */
